WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.320
The most traumatic thing I remember at Audrey was a man coming to me with this story, he said,

2
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:18.620
"I just found my little girl's leg and we want to keep it until we find the rest of her body,

3
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.400
so they can be buried together."

4
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.140
And I cried.

5
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.440
But you say they found that little girl?

6
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:25.640
Yeah.

7
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:27.620
But some of them they didn't.

8
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.520
Of course, they had mass graves, you know.

9
00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:32.660
They ended up having to bury those people.

10
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:44.980
And I understood from Red Cross that lots of people—that were so poor that they couldn't afford a funeral—did not identify their bodies when they knew it,

11
00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.140
because they knew they couldn't afford to bury them.

12
00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.570
I think that's sadder than anything.
